te is fully developed. In contrast, B: f1-c4 is a developing move that increases pressure without committing the pawn structure.\n\nReason:  \nB: f1-c4 develops a piece to an active square, targets the vulnerable f7 square, improves coordination, and keeps flexibility in the center. It avoids premature pawn advances and enhances attacking chances without risk.\n\nAnswer: B: f1-c4"}
